Cell["Extract Individual Thermocouple Type Data Sets", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9492293227976294`*^9, 
  3.949229346973674*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e4cf2456-ce5f-4aaa-8295-\
13407b3636fd"],

Cell["\<\
Note that the data start at row 6. The first thing we need to do is to \
convert from the Tabular column to a list using Normal[]. If you scroll down \
the Tabular data set shown above you will see blank cells. We need to exclude \
these and use DeleteMissing[] for this. We also have to convert the cells \
from strings to numbers and use ToExpression[] for this: \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.949229358676663*^9, 3.9492293659639187`*^9}, {
  3.949255468868022*^9, 3.949255549768921*^9}, {3.9492555905245533`*^9, 
