Cell["\<\
This shows that we our interpolating function passes through all the data \
points. Values in between the original data points are determined via linear \
interpolation between the 2 immediately adjacent data points unless a higher \
order interpolation function is requested (e.g., splines or Hermite \
polynomials).\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9493308477642*^9, 3.949330857676011*^9}, {
  3.949339678823028*^9, 3.949339680037125*^9}, {3.9493417194361477`*^9, 
