Cell["\<\
This exactly the function we need in practice where we have measured the \
thermocouple voltage and now want to predict the temperature that generated \
it.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.949342576206332*^9, 3.949342621108426*^9}, {
  3.949344579837872*^9, 
  3.949344583600533*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e03755d4-758e-4db8-bcfe-\
a1a639ebf6aa"],

Cell["\<\
For example if we were to boil some water and record the temperature with a \
type K thermocouple and measure 4.1 mV then the corresponding temperature \
would be (in \[Degree]C):\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.981452071124991*^9, 3.981452152864149*^9}, 
   3.981452238106214*^9},ExpressionUUID->"387fe71d-4bf8-4f77-be27-\
2769cb1daef4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"interpolatingFnInv", "[", "4.1", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9814520391751127`*^9, 3.9814520597415333`*^9}},
